id: pm-4euctr
title: "GH-1500: Preserve null, empty and reserved JSON row facts through host rendering"
description: "TOON compaction removes present null/empty row cells before table encoding, which labels them absent and disagrees with the JSON result. Preserve row value semantics and avoid unnecessary absent metadata while retaining genuinely missing-key encoding."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-10-18T21:45:34.695Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:20.064Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:18.963Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:18.963Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Public rendering round trips explicit null, empty, missing and nested row values without classifying present cells as absent; Context-shaped scalar tables avoid redundant cell metadata; Ordinary lean JSON semantics and JSON envelopes remain compatible; Regression fails before the fix and passes with exact final-byte budget accounting; Host compaction preserves reserved JSON row keys through TOON and retains their nonempty values in explicit lean JSON without mutating input"
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Preserved explicit nulls, empty containers, empty rows and reserved JSON keys through host compaction while retaining compatible lean JSON and compact successful health diagnostics."
expected_result: "Context and table rows retain selected JSON facts without false absence labels or input mutation, and existing health budgets and JSON contracts remain valid."
actual_result: "Pre-fix regressions detected null/empty and reserved-key losses. Final 110 primary tests, all 32 token surfaces, linked row tests, packed consumers, TypeScript and the full static gate pass. Final-head source coverage and reviews are enforced before merge."
